    "summary": "Complete exam-ready guide to CAG & Constitutional Bodies.",
    "body": "<div class=\"title-banner\">\n    <h1>Chapters 13, 14 & 15</h1>\n    <h2>CAG & Constitutional Bodies • DPSP • Anti-Defection Law</h2>\n    <div class=\"tagline\">Three Chapters — One Complete Guide</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"section\">\n    <div class=\"section-title t-teal\">📚 What's Inside?</div>\n    <div class=\"box box-teal\">\n      <div class=\"box-title\">📖 Chapter 13: CAG & Other Constitutional Bodies</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>⚖️ Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) — Article 148</li>\n        <li>🏛️ UPSC, Finance Commission, Attorney General</li>\n        <li>👥 NHRC, CVC, CIC</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"box box-navy\">\n      <div class=\"box-title\">📖 Chapter 14: Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP)</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>📜 Part IV (Articles 36 to 51)</li>\n        <li>🎯 Socialist, Gandhian, Liberal-Intellectual Principles</li>\n        <li>⚖️ Difference between FR and DPSP</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"box box-purple\">\n      <div class=\"box-title\">📖 Chapter 15: Anti-Defection Law & 10th Schedule</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>🚫 10th Schedule (52nd Amendment, 1988)</li>\n        <li>📋 Grounds for Disqualification</li>\n        <li>⚖️ Landmark Cases — Kihoto Hollohan</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"simple\">\n      Three important chapters merged — Constitutional Bodies, DPSP, and Anti-Defection Law. All in one colorful guide.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"section\">\n    <div class=\"section-title t-navy\">⚖️ 13.1 The Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) — Article 148</div>\n    <h3>📌 Appointment and Qualifications</h3>\n    <table class=\"table-navy\">\n      <tr><th>📌 Feature</th><th>💬 Detail</th></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Article</strong></td><td><span class=\"hl-navy\">148</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Appointment</strong></td><td>By the President</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Qualifications</strong></td><td>Not specified in the Constitution (Convention: senior IAAS officer)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Term</strong></td><td><span class=\"hl-teal\">6 years</span> or until age 65 years, whichever is earlier</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Resignation</strong></td><td>Addressed to the President</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Removal</strong></td><td>Same as a Supreme Court Judge (Impeachment by 2/3rd majority of both Houses)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>First CAG of India</strong></td><td>V. Narahari Rao</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Current CAG (2025)</strong></td><td>K. Sanjay Murthy</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <h3>⚡ Powers and Functions of CAG</h3>\n    <table class=\"table-teal\">\n      <tr><th>Function</th><th>Detail</th></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Audit of Accounts</strong></td><td>Audits all accounts of the Union and States.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Audit of PSUs</strong></td><td>Audits government companies and corporations.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Advisory Role</strong></td><td>Advises the President/Governor on matters of accounts.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Report Submission</strong></td><td>Submits audit reports to the President/Governor, who places them before Parliament/State Legislature.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Public Accounts Committee</strong></td><td>Assists the PAC in examining the CAG's reports.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Compilation of Accounts</strong></td><td>Compiles and maintains accounts of the Union and States.</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <div class=\"keypoint\">\n      <strong>KEY POINT:</strong> The CAG is called the <span class=\"hl-teal\">\"Guardian of Public Purse\"</span> and the <span class=\"hl-navy\">\"Friend, Philosopher, and Guide\"</span> of the Public Accounts Committee.\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"simple\">\n      CAG = The auditor of India. Checks how government spends money. Called \"Guardian of Public Purse.\"\n    </div>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"section\">\n    <div class=\"section-title t-purple\">🏛️ 13.2 Other Constitutional Bodies</div>\n    <h3>🏛️ 13.2.1 Union Public Service Commission (UPSC)</h3>\n    <table class=\"table-purple\">\n      <tr><th>📌 Feature</th><th>💬 Detail</th></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Article</strong></td><td>315 to 323</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Established</strong></td><td>1926 (Originally Federal Public Service Commission)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Appointment</strong></td><td>By the President</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Members</strong></td><td>1 Chairman + 10 Members (maximum)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Term</strong></td><td>6 years or until age 65 years</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Functions</strong></td><td>Conducts Civil Services Examination, Engineering Services, etc.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>First Chairman</strong></td><td>Sir Ross Barker</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <h3>💰 13.2.2 Finance Commission</h3>\n    <table class=\"table-amber\">\n      <tr><th>📌 Feature</th><th>💬 Detail</th></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Article</strong></td><td>280</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Appointment</strong></td><td>By the President every 5 years</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Composition</strong></td><td>1 Chairman + 4 Members</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Functions</strong></td><td>Recommends distribution of taxes between Centre and States.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>First Finance Commission</strong></td><td>1951 (Chairman: K.C. Neogy)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Current (16th) Finance Commission</strong></td><td>Chairman: Arvind Panagariya (2024)</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <h3>⚖️ 13.2.3 Attorney General of India</h3>\n    <table class=\"table-sky\">\n      <tr><th>📌 Feature</th><th>💬 Detail</th></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Article</strong></td><td>76</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Appointment</strong></td><td>By the President</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Qualifications</strong></td><td>Qualified to be a Supreme Court Judge</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Term</strong></td><td>Not fixed (during pleasure of President)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Role</strong></td><td>Chief Legal Advisor to Government of India</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>First AG</strong></td><td>M.C. Setalvad</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Current AG (2025)</strong></td><td>R. Venkataramani</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <div class=\"simple\">\n      UPSC = 315, Finance Commission = 280, Attorney General = 76. All appointed by President.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"section\">\n    <div class=\"section-title t-green\">👥 13.2.4 - 13.2.7 Other Bodies"
