    "id": "polity-ch16",
    "subject": "Polity",
    "chapterNo": 16,
    "title": "Panchayati Raj & Municipalities",
    "date": "2026-09-16",
    "readTime": "16 min",
    "icon": "🌾",
    "tags": [
      "73rd",
      "74th",
      "Amendment"
    ],
    "summary": "Complete exam-ready guide to Panchayati Raj & Municipalities.",
    "body": "<div class=\"title-banner\">\n    <span class=\"crown\">📘</span>\n    <span class=\"shield\">🇮🇳</span>\n    <h1>Chapters 16, 17 & 18</h1>\n    <h2>PANCHAYATI RAJ • AMENDMENTS • ARTICLES & SCHEDULES</h2>\n    <div class=\"tagline\">Complete Full Notes</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"section\">\n    <div class=\"section-title t-brown\">📚 What's Inside?</div>\n    <div class=\"box box-brown\">\n      <div class=\"box-title\">📖 Chapter 16: Panchayati Raj & Municipalities</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>🌾 73rd Amendment (Panchayats) — Part IX, 11th Schedule</li>\n        <li>🏙️ 74th Amendment (Municipalities) — Part IX-A, 12th Schedule</li>\n        <li>📝 Previous Year Questions</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"box box-amber\">\n      <div class=\"box-title\">📖 Chapter 17: Important Constitutional Amendments</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>⚡ 1st, 7th, 42nd, 44th, 52nd, 61st Amendments</li>\n        <li>🎯 73rd, 74th, 86th, 91st Amendments</li>\n        <li>💰 101st (GST), 103rd (EWS), 106th (Women's Reservation)</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"box box-purple\">\n      <div class=\"box-title\">📖 Chapter 18: Important Articles & Schedules</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>📜 70+ Important Articles (Article 1 to 368)</li>\n        <li>📋 12 Schedules (1st to 12th)</li>\n        <li>📝 Quick Revision Tables for SSC</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"simple\">\n      Three chapters merged — Complete detailed notes for final revision before exams.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"section\">\n    <div class=\"section-title t-green\">🌾 16.1 Panchayati Raj — 73rd Amendment Act, 1992</div>\n    <div class=\"essay\">\n      <p>The <strong>73rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992</strong> gave constitutional status to Panchayati Raj institutions. It added <span class=\"hl-green\">Part IX</span> to the Constitution and the <span class=\"hl-teal\">11th Schedule</span>.</p>\n    </div>\n    <table class=\"table-green\">\n      <tr><th>📌 Feature</th><th>💬 Detail</th></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Part Added</strong></td><td><span class=\"hl-green\">Part IX</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Articles</strong></td><td>243 to 243O</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Schedule</strong></td><td><span class=\"hl-green\">11th Schedule (29 subjects)</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Came Into Force</strong></td><td>24th April 1993</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Three-Tier System</strong></td><td>Gram Panchayat (Village), Panchayat Samiti (Block), Zila Parishad (District)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Reservation</strong></td><td>SC/ST in proportion to population; Women — <span class=\"hl-pink\">1/3rd</span></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Term</strong></td><td>5 years</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>State Election Commission</strong></td><td>Conducts Panchayat elections</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>State Finance Commission</strong></td><td>Constituted every 5 years</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>First State to Implement</strong></td><td>Rajasthan (1959)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>First State After Amendment</strong></td><td>Madhya Pradesh (1994)</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <div class=\"keypoint\">\n      <strong>KEY POINT:</strong> States with population <span class=\"hl-amber\">less than 20 lakh</span> may not have the intermediate (block) level.\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"simple\">\n      73rd Amendment = Gave constitutional status to Panchayats. 3-tier system: Village → Block → District. 11th Schedule has 29 subjects.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"section\">\n    <div class=\"section-title t-teal\">🌾 16.1 Panchayati Raj — Powers & 11th Schedule</div>\n    <h3>⚡ Powers and Functions</h3>\n    <div class=\"box box-teal\">\n      <ul>\n        <li>📋 <strong>Mandatory Functions:</strong> Agriculture, land improvement, minor irrigation, rural housing, drinking water, roads, education, health, etc.</li>\n        <li>💰 <strong>Financial Powers:</strong> Can levy taxes, tolls, and fees. Receive grants from State and Central governments.</li>\n        <li>🏦 <strong>State Finance Commission:</strong> Constituted every 5 years to review the financial position of Panchayats.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <h3>📜 11th Schedule (29 Subjects)</h3>\n    <table class=\"table-teal\">\n      <tr><th>#</th><th>Subject</th><th>#</th><th>Subject</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>1</td><td>Agriculture</td><td>16</td><td>Poverty alleviation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>2</td><td>Land improvement</td><td>17</td><td>Education (primary & secondary)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>3</td><td>Minor irrigation</td><td>18</td><td>Technical training</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>4</td><td>Rural housing</td><td>19</td><td>Adult education</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>5</td><td>Drinking water</td><td>20</td><td>Libraries</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>6</td><td>Roads and bridges</td><td>21</td><td>Cultural activities</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>7</td><td>Health and sanitation</td><td>22</td><td>Markets and fairs</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>8</td><td>Women and child development</td><td>23</td><td>Rural electrification</td></tr>\n    </table>\n    <div class=\"simple\">\n      Panchayats handle 29 subjects — water, roads, education, health, agriculture, and more.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"section\">\n    <div class=\"section-title t-sky\">🏙️ 16.2 Municipalities — 74th Amendment Act, 1992</div>\n    <div class=\"essay\">\n      <p>The <strong>74th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992</strong> gave constitutional status to Municipalities. It added <span class=\"hl-sky\">Part IX-A</span> to the Constitution and the <span class=\"hl-navy\">12th Schedule</span>.</p>"
